<title>USA: Summary of FY98 ag fund bills OKed by US Congress.</title>
<headline>Summary of FY98 ag fund bills OKed by US Congress.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here are highlights of the fiscal 1998 agriculture appropriations bill passed Thursday by the U.S. Senate and House with comparisons to White House requests and current funding:</p>
<p>The Senate bill offers $50.7 billion, the House bill provides $49.6 billion. For FY97, $53.9 billion was provided.</p>
<p> Program (Mln $)  House   Senate   Request    FY97</p>
<p> EEP		    205	150	 500	10</p>
<p> GSM 102, 103     5,700    5,700     5,700   3,500</p>
<p> PL-480		 879	889	 870     880</p>
<p> Mkt Access Prog     90	 90	  90     N/A</p>
<p> FSIS		   589	591	 591     574</p>
<p> Child nutrition  7,767    7,769     7,783   8,653</p>
<p> WIC		  3,924    3,927     4,108   3,805</p>
<p> Food stamps     25,140   26,051    27,551  27,618</p>
<p> FDA-A		  872	949	 988     921</p>
<p> CFTC		    57	 60	  60	55</p>
<p> Farm Credit Admin   34	 34	  34	37</p>
<p> Total	     49,447   50,685   52,302   53,889</p>
<p>A-House did not allow $91 million in prescription drug user fees for FY98; Senate did.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
</text>
